[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4245735772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117782#issuecomment-4245735772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117782","id":4245735772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79EMlc","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T17:02:27Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T17:02:27Z","body":"> I'm currently not entirely sure how to add echo events for axes in a way that makes sense, but I was also thinking of creating another project setting that would be a deadzone for echo events. If the axis value is higher than the deadzone, the echo events will be sent.\r\n\r\nI would just reuse the same deadzone as the regular action. If you hold an axis at a position where the input would be sent, it should also echo eventually.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4245735772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4245748118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117782#issuecomment-4245748118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117782","id":4245748118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79EPmW","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T17:04:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T17:04:48Z","body":"> > I'm currently not entirely sure how to add echo events for axes in a way that makes sense, but I was also thinking of creating another project setting that would be a deadzone for echo events. If the axis value is higher than the deadzone, the echo events will be sent.\r\n> \r\n> I would just reuse the same deadzone as the regular action. If you hold an axis at a position where the input would be sent, it should also echo eventually.\r\n\r\nBut the thing is, `InputEvent`s don't depend on actions, it's the actions that depend on `InputEvent`s, as far as I know. 😅 \r\nAnd different input actions can contain similar axis events, which will create some ambiguity (what action should we choose for the deadzone?).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4245748118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390638550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117782#issuecomment-4390638550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117782","id":4390638550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBbPT1g","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T17:55:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T17:55:22Z","body":"Although now that I think about it, should we really have axis echo events? I mean, they have to share the same deadzone for all actions, otherwise we have to introduce a different type of echo events (most likely `InputEventAction`, and we will have to modify its documentation to say that it *is* sent by the engine in case of echo events). If neither approach is good enough, I'm not sure how we can make axis echo events :( ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390638550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4788608573","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117782#issuecomment-4788608573","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117782","id":4788608573,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHWxePQ","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T11:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T11:11:25Z","body":"I decided to remove joypad axis echo events for now, I think we need to discuss this part more since there are several approaches to do it.\r\n\r\n> Tested locally, it mostly works as expected.\r\n> \r\n> Some feedback:\r\n> \r\n> * Echo events don't work for focus navigation, or Tree/ItemList navigation. I would expect echo events to be followed in both cases to match other games/engines.\r\n>   \r\n>   * In contrast, it works with keyboard-based navigation (try holding down Tab).\r\n\r\nThat's strange, because button echo events for just fine for me. Did you try to use the sticks for navigation? In that case, yes, they weren't supposed to work at the moment, and now they're removed, so I think it's hopefully not a problem for now. :D\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c81d3c06-2bd7-4fcb-84a8-9b20e1b190e3\r\n\r\n> * The repeat timer should ignore `Engine.time_scale`, as currently, using a higher time scale will speed up the rate at which echo events are sent (as well as reduce the initial delay before the first echo event). You can test this by using `--time-scale 5` in the **Main Run Args** project setting.\r\n\r\nFixed!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4788608573/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5995375960","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117782#issuecomment-5995375960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117782","id":5995375960,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZVotWA","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T13:24:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T13:24:39Z","body":"Now that I think about it, I think I should change the way the GUI elements that have their own joypad \"echo\" events work with this PR (if I remember correctly, those are `Tree` and `OptionButton`, but may be more), so they don't generate their own events and react to the ones.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5995375960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]